[size=5][b]QuickStash[/b][/size]

Press [b]G[/b] and everything in your backpack that a nearby container already holds goes into that container. No windows, no dragging.

It is the game's own "move all similar items" chest button, applied to every container in the area at once.

[line]

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Moves every stackable item from your backpack into nearby containers that already contain the same item. Nearest container first.
[*]Items inside bags in your backpack (farming bag and so on) are included.
[*]Shows a small bubble above each container with the items that went in, in the same style as the workstation craft bubble.
[*]Plays the item sound and shows "Stashed N items" on screen.
[*]Works while you are walking.
[/list]

[size=4][b]What it never touches[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Your toolbelt and equipped gear.
[*]The item you carry over your head.
[*]Tools, weapons and the bags themselves. Only stackable items move.
[*]Containers with item filters only receive what they accept (firewood sheds, wells, ore pallets...).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Which containers count as "nearby"[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Inside a work zone: every storage container of that zone. These are the same containers the chest window lists as zone storage.
[*]Anywhere else: storage containers within a configurable radius around you.
[/list]

[size=4][b]It will not fire while[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]a window is open (chest, inventory, menus),
[*]the game is paused,
[*]your controls are disabled (cutscenes, dialogs).
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/graveyardkeeper2/mods/48]BepInEx for Graveyard Keeper 2[/url] (BepInEx 5)
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[b]Vortex:[/b] use the "Mod Manager Download" button, enable, deploy.
[b]Manual:[/b] extract the archive into the game folder so that the file ends up at
[code]Graveyard Keeper 2\BepInEx\plugins\QuickStash\QuickStash.dll[/code]

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]
Run the game once, then edit
[code]Graveyard Keeper 2\BepInEx\config\com.caiotoon.gk2.quickstash.cfg[/code]
Changes apply within a second while the game is running. No restart needed.

[list]
[*][b]StashKey[/b] (G): the hotkey. Modifiers are supported, for example [i]G + LeftShift[/i].
[*][b]IncludeBagContents[/b] (true): also stash items stored inside bags in the backpack.
[*][b]PlaySound[/b] (true): sound on stash.
[*][b]ShowBubbles[/b] (true): bubble above containers that received items.
[*][b]BubbleSeconds[/b] (2): how long the bubble stays.
[*][b]BubbleScale[/b] (0.6): bubble size. 1 is the size of the craft bubble.
[*][b]BubbleColumns[/b] (2): cells per row. 0 picks automatically: 2 columns when the scale is 0.5 or lower, else 1.
[*][b]BubbleSpacing[/b] (-1): gap between cells. Negative uses the game's own spacing.
[*][b]MaxBubbleItems[/b] (4): how many items a bubble shows, largest stacks first.
[*][b]ShowBubbleCount[/b] (false): show the amount on each cell.
[*][b]FallbackRadius[/b] (12): search radius used outside work zones.
[*][b]IncludeConveyorChests[/b] (false): also stash into conveyor chests.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Keyboard only. G is not used by the game's default bindings.
[*]An item only moves if the container already holds at least one of it. Star quality counts as a different item, as in the base game.
[*]Safe to add or remove at any time. The mod stores nothing in your save.
[*]Co-op: if the game ever enables it, the hotkey only works for the host.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
No game files are replaced. One small patch adds the bubble to the game's object bubbles. Inventory size mods and other BepInEx plugins should work alongside it.

[size=4][b]Source code[/b][/size]
[url=https://github.com/caiotoon/CaioToOn-GK2-Mods]github.com/caiotoon/CaioToOn-GK2-Mods[/url]
Bug reports and suggestions are welcome here in the comments or as GitHub issues.
